; Re-expose the vendored emulator's core as the `emu` library in our project — the
; two halves the CIL backend needs:
;   - Emu.Risc5_isa : the shared instr encoding (the backend's *emit* target)
;   - Emu.Risc      : the interpreter (the differential jig's *execution* engine)
; The emulator arrives as oberon-risc-hardcaml's OWN nested submodule (one pin,
; owned by the host repo — its lockstep oracle keeps the emulator consistent with
; the design; init with `git submodule update --init --recursive`). Its library is
; private behind its dune-project boundary, so we copy its lib/ sources here and
; compile them (the same trick the host repo's `oracle` uses, which keeps the
; submodule untouched). Warnings off (-w -a): vendored code, not ours to lint.
; Only dependency is unix, matching the emulator's own lib/dune.

(copy_files ../oberon-risc-hardcaml/vendor/oberon-risc-emu-ocaml/lib/*.ml)

(copy_files ../oberon-risc-hardcaml/vendor/oberon-risc-emu-ocaml/lib/*.mli)

(library
 (name emu)
 (libraries unix)
 (flags
  (:standard -w -a)))
